			"date": "2023-03-14T17:27:44.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> that's interesting, because it simultaneously seems to highlight where the bottleneck is and you'd think get it lots of investment.  Maybe those pages would otherwise render not a lot until all those spinners were done minus some round trip latency? Or more likely if that was the option, they just wouldn't be on the web maybe?</p>",
