			"author": {
				"name": "Evan B🥥ehs",
				"url": "https://social.coop/@eb",
				"avatarUrl": "https://cdn.masto.host/fediversezachleatcom/cache/accounts/avatars/109/403/079/868/456/691/original/f41d3e92406d02c0.jpeg"
			},
			"date": "2023-03-15T22:27:56.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> hot take for the DMs of static site generator man... But I disagree.</p><p>I mean, my server can process requests in as little as 1ms, but the network overhead of what... 80ms minimum? Means a performant client side router will win. Not to mention, whenever you click a link without that routing the browser needs to redo it's CSS JavaScript ect shenanigans.</p><p>Look, my point is that for *applications*, CSR can be good, so long as it's respectful of bundle size, is optimised, and has SSR</p>",
			"via": "fediverse"
		},
